* ============================================================================
* bbs_mail_check.dts -- the house reads its own mail (AIF-108 M1 step 1, made
* STANDING by owner ruling 2026-08-12: "a scheduled task").
*
* Origin: the challenge lane's first act was reading the boards, and the read
* found an assignment four days stale ([assign:grok] Lane 1 write adapter M2)
* and an untriaged defect report ("descending path looks off"). The lesson
* was written before the evidence arrived: "a submission protocol without a
* reading habit is a drop box." This script is the reading habit.
*
* Runs headless via the DotTalkBBSMail scheduled task (register script:
* register-bbs-mailcheck.ps1, host side, alongside the development root),
* which appends stdout to _bbsd_logs\bbs_mail.log under the host log root
* -- the same cmd-redirect pattern the bbsd
* task uses (ALTERNATE not needed; the wrapper owns capture. DOTSCRIPT OUT
* is NOT used: AIF-081 measured it losing the entire cmdout surface).
*
* The board list below mirrors the seeded rooms. A new board must be added
* here to be watched -- acceptable for now; a BBS READ ALL verb would retire
* the list (named small gap, not built here).
*
* Reading the log: newest run is at the bottom; runs are delimited by the
* FORMULA markers. Anything between them that is not seeded content is MAIL.
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

FORMULA "BBS-MAIL-CHECK-BEGIN"
VERSION

BBS BOARDS
BBS READ board.governance
BBS READ board.afb.chat
BBS READ board.notice
BBS READ board.lounge
BBS READ board.guestbook
BBS READ board.worklog

FORMULA "BBS-MAIL-CHECK-END"
